Libraries tools/patch-live.py copies into push3_opt/push3/lib/xkbcommon. The
shim (standalone.cpp, loadXkbcommon) loads them only when the system has no
libxkbcommon-x11; otherwise the system's own pair is used.

libxkbcommon.so.0, libxkbcommon-x11.so.0: xkbcommon 1.5.0 from Debian 12
(packages libxkbcommon0 and libxkbcommon-x11-0 1.5.0-1 from deb.debian.org
over HTTPS, matching the SHA256 in bookworm's Packages index:
e3fe045b9a33a101de1c5a912a4a10928db055c3f68930f47eccbb44d7c7d54e and
9b34d760f0ca0f125419a6becc6492c489f0371953ef42caad3401199a497ff5).
libxkbcommon-x11 builds keymaps with libxkbcommon's internal structures, so the
two must be the same version: Arch's x11 part (1.13) with Ubuntu's libxkbcommon
(1.6) crashed Live on the first key press. These need glibc 2.33, below Live's
own 2.35; Arch's and Ubuntu 24.04's builds need 2.38 (for __isoc23_strtol).

innoextract: innoextract 1.10-dev (git 6e9e34e, github.com/dscharrer/innoextract,
zlib licence, LICENSE.innoextract), for install.sh. Live 12.4's Windows installer is Inno Setup 6.4
(setup data version 6.4.0.1), which innoextract 1.9, the release most
distributions ship (Ubuntu, Mint, Debian, Fedora), cannot read. Boost,
libstdc++ and libgcc are linked in; it needs glibc 2.35, liblzma.so.5,
libz.so.1 and libbz2.so.1.0 (install.sh links libbz2.so.1 under that name on
Fedora and openSUSE). Built with Arch's Boost 1.92 static libraries and the
AUR package's boost1.89.0.patch:
  g++ -O2 -c ../innoextract-compat.cpp -o ic.o
  g++ -O2 -c ../../shim/glibccompat.cpp -o gc.o   (wic_unpacked/shim)
  cmake <src> -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DUSE_STATIC_LIBS=OFF -DBoost_USE_STATIC_LIBS=ON \
      -DUSE_LTO=OFF -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF \
      -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS="$PWD/ic.o $PWD/gc.o -static-libstdc++ -static-libgcc -Wl,--as-needed -s"
  make
(innoextract-compat.cpp: arc4random, GLIBC_2.36 in Arch's static Boost.Random;
glibccompat.cpp: the C23 strtoul and sscanf of glibc 2.38 headers.)

openssl3/libssl.so.3, openssl3/libcrypto.so.3: OpenSSL 3.0.22 from Debian 12
(package libssl3 3.0.22-1~deb12u2 from security.debian.org over HTTPS, matching
the SHA256 in bookworm-security's Packages index:
cb4784740daa9b3b0eaea2b444bbefa686794afbbf3d678d238c1fd9875f2efd; Apache
License 2.0, openssl3/LICENSE.openssl). Live 12 needs these two names to start
but calls nothing in them; install.sh copies them to compat_lib/openssl3 and the
launcher adds that folder only when the system has no OpenSSL 3 (Fedora 45 ships
OpenSSL 4 only), so a plug-in that uses OpenSSL 3 gets a maintained build. They
need glibc 2.34. Debian's build looks for its configuration and CA certificates
under /usr/lib/ssl (Debian's layout); libcurl and most plug-ins name their own.
Update with Debian's next security release.

libxml2/libxml2.so.2: libxml2 2.9.13 from Ubuntu 22.04 (package libxml2
2.9.13+dfsg-1ubuntu0.14 from security.ubuntu.com over HTTPS, matching the SHA256
in jammy-security's Packages index, whose own SHA256 matches InRelease:
16e395b2c52d6ab232053468febc69f0876956ec2fae357a941a2a8dab36574f; MIT licence,
libxml2/LICENSE.libxml2). Max's maxxslt extension needs libxml2.so.2; Arch and
other current distributions have libxml2.so.16 only, and the Max window showed
"libxml2.so.2: cannot open shared object file". It needs ICU 70 (compat_lib has
it for Live 12), zlib, liblzma and glibc 2.34; install.sh copies it to
compat_lib/libxml2, which the launcher uses only when the system has no
libxml2.so.2.

libxml2-icu66/libxml2.so.2: libxml2 2.9.10 from Ubuntu 20.04, for Live 11 (package
libxml2 2.9.10+dfsg-5ubuntu0.20.04.10 from security.ubuntu.com over HTTPS, SHA256
90145086978f8eb6253621eea93dd1fb144ff6475a17507e467557d63d427e7f, matching
focal-security's Packages index, whose own SHA256 matches InRelease; MIT licence,
libxml2-icu66/LICENSE.libxml2). Same purpose as libxml2/ above, but built against ICU 66,
which Live 11's compat_lib has (Live 11's image has no ICU 70). Ubuntu 20.04's standard
support ended in 2025: this is its last public build. Only Max's maxxslt loads it, and
only where the system has no libxml2.so.2. install.sh copies it to compat_lib/libxml2 for
Live 11.
